	abstract = {A new mother wavelet function for extended X-ray absorption fine-structure (EXAFS) data analysis has been designed, combining a model EXAFS function derived from the ıt ab initio EXAFS code ıt FEFF8.20 and the complex Morlet wavelet. This new ıt FEFF–Morlet mother wavelet routine allows the generation of wavelets well adapted to specific EXAFS problems. A substantial gain in resolution of the wavelet ridges in ıt k and ıt r space is achieved. The method is applied to a structural problem of Zn–Al double-layer hydroxides, demonstrating unequivocally the homogeneity of the metal cation distribution in the hydroxide layers.},
